1
00:00:03,450 --> 00:00:06,290
(Sheldon:)All right, I'm ready
for my next question.

2
00:00:06,290 --> 00:00:10,040
(Amy:)In a world where rhinoceroses
are domesticated pets,

3
00:00:10,040 --> 00:00:12,040
(Amy:)who wins the Second World War?

4
00:00:14,350 --> 00:00:16,250
(Sheldon:)Uganda.

5
00:00:16,250 --> 00:00:17,250
(Amy:)Defend.

6
00:00:17,250 --> 00:00:19,100
(Sheldon:)Kenya rises to power

7
00:00:19,100 --> 00:00:20,720
(Sheldon:)on the export of rhinoceroses.

8
00:00:20,720 --> 00:00:22,920
(Sheldon:)A Central African
power block is formed,

9
00:00:22,920 --> 00:00:25,020
(Sheldon:)colonizing North Africa and Europe.

10
00:00:25,020 --> 00:00:28,440
(Sheldon:)When war breaks out, no one can
afford the luxury of a rhino.

11
00:00:28,440 --> 00:00:30,830
(Sheldon:)Kenya withers, Uganda triumphs.

12
00:00:32,860 --> 00:00:33,950
(Amy:)Correct.

13
00:00:33,950 --> 00:00:35,270
(Amy:)My turn.

14
00:00:36,930 --> 00:00:41,310
(Sheldon:)In a world where a piano is a weapon,
not a musical instrument,

15
00:00:41,310 --> 00:00:45,090
(Sheldon:)on what does Scott Joplin
play "The Maple Leaf Rag"?

16
00:00:45,090 --> 00:00:47,880
(Amy:)Tuned bayonets.

17
00:00:47,880 --> 00:00:48,950
(Amy:)Defend.

18
00:00:48,950 --> 00:00:49,880
(Amy:)Isn't it obvious?

19
00:00:49,880 --> 00:00:52,450
(Sheldon:)You're right. My apologies.

20
00:00:53,950 --> 00:00:57,470
(Leonard:)What the hell are you guys playing?

21
00:00:57,470 --> 00:00:59,220
(Sheldon:)It's a game we invented.

22
00:00:59,220 --> 00:01:01,430
(Sheldon:)It's called Counterfactuals.

